$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=progpel  LOC_AFTER=?

* A prime divides the sifting product exactly when it is at most the sifting level and does not divide the modulus.

s1::simpr |- ( ( ( M e. ( ZZ>= ` 2 ) /\ Z e. NN /\ N e. NN0 ) /\ Q e. Prime ) -> Q e. Prime )
